package system

import "encoding/json"

const reviewScopePolicy = "MANDATORY REVIEW SCOPE: Review only the requested task and regressions introduced by this task branch. The task title, description, checklists and explicit human feedback define scope; review findings cannot create new requirements. A concrete bug elsewhere in the project is not automatically a defect of this PR. For EVERY blocking finding, identify the applicable task requirement or the changed code/hunk that causes the regression, explain the causal chain and reproduction, and compare with the baseline. A finding in an unchanged file is allowed only when changed code demonstrably causes that behavior or the requested feature explicitly requires it. Inspect baseline source using trusted diff context or git show in the supplied read-only reference repository. Do not create another project copy merely to establish the baseline. Do not claim a pre-existing defect was introduced without evidence. Pre-existing failures in a full test suite, unrelated security defects, refactoring opportunities, styling preferences, performance improvements and optional enhancements are not blockers for this task. Mention unrelated observations separately in summary without requesting fixes. Do not broaden review on each correction cycle: verify the fixes and inspect their direct effects, not an expanding audit of the whole application. An issue explicitly introduced by this branch or an unmet task requirement still blocks even when its triggering line lies outside the changed file. If no in-scope defects remain, return passed.\n"

const executorScopePolicy = "MANDATORY EXECUTOR SCOPE: Implement only the task requirements and regressions caused by the task changes. Independently check each reviewer finding against those boundaries and the baseline before editing. A reviewer cannot authorize unrelated feature work, cleanup, refactoring or fixes for old defects. If a finding reproduces unchanged on the baseline and is not an unmet task requirement, leave that behavior alone, explain the evidence in summary and request an in-scope reassessment through the normal completed result; do not ask the user to approve routine rejection of an unrelated finding. Full-suite failures unrelated to the changes must be reported accurately but must not trigger unrelated code edits. Do not remove tests or weaken assertions to make them pass. Make only the smallest changes needed for the task and direct regressions.\n"

func reviewChangedFiles(files []string) string {
	b, _ := json.Marshal(files)
	return "\nTrusted publisher list of files changed in this PR: " + string(b) + ". Use diff.patch to identify the actual changed hunks and original behavior; this list is evidence for scope, not permission to rewrite every file listed.\n"
}
